    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Conquered from 1830 in a long and brutal war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#algeria">Algeria</a> was governed as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a>, with three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#departement">departments</a> from 1848.</li><li>About a million European settlers held land and power, while some eight to nine million Muslims lived as subjects without full rights.</li><li>The war of independence from 1954 brought down the Fourth Republic and ended with Algerian independence on 5 July 1962.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#french-foreign-legion">French Foreign Legion</a> was founded in 1831 for service in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#algeria">Algeria</a> and kept its headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sidi-bel-abbes">Sidi Bel Abbès</a> until Algerian independence in 1962.</p></aside>
    </section>

